# Byte-compiled Python. .github/check-english.py and its self-test are run
# straight from the checkout, and CPython writes a __pycache__ next to the
# source the moment anything imports or compiles it. One of those .pyc files
# was committed by a broad `git add` on 2026-09-20: a binary blob, pinned to
# one interpreter version, stale the moment the script next changes, and
# re-staged on every local run. Nothing in this repository is built, so
# nothing byte-compiled belongs in it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Editor and OS droppings that a broad `git add` sweeps in the same way.
.DS_Store
*.swp
